WEBVTT

00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:13,380
What are the acceptable forms of B12 for cancer patients?

00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:17,100
Remember, we'll try to stay away from methylated supplements,

00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:20,260
unless you have elevated homocysteine.

00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:22,380
So if you do not have elevated homocysteine,

00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:26,420
but you have cancer, what is it acceptable for it would be 12?

00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:30,500
You want to take hydroxychombolamine

00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:33,020
as typically the one that we use.

00:00:35,270 --> 00:00:37,270
But, uh,

00:00:37,270 --> 00:00:41,270
professional health products has a pro-hydroxychombolamine.

00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:46,190
Seeking health has a hydroxychombolamine.

00:00:46,190 --> 00:00:49,750
You can also use a denticel-chombolamine.

00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:53,270
Seeking health has a denticel-slash-hydroxy,

00:00:53,270 --> 00:00:55,430
so it's 50-50 blend.

00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:57,590
I'm not sure that that's necessary.

00:00:57,590 --> 00:01:00,630
Typically, people take hydroxychombolamine.

